# gate-selfcheck G-E — known-benign secret-sweep matches.
#
# Format:  <repo-basename>/<path-glob>   # why this is not a credential
# The reason is MANDATORY. A bare entry is reported as ALLOW-NOREASON, because an
# exemption nobody justified is indistinguishable from an oversight six weeks later.
# Suppression is never silent: gate-selfcheck always prints how many hits this file ate.
#
# Add an entry ONLY after you have looked at the match and can say, in writing, why it
# cannot be a live credential. "It's in a fork" is not a reason. "It's an upstream unit
# test's generated PEM fixture, verified <date>" is.
#
# Established 2026-08-08 (S44) after the first full-corpus sweep: 43 hits, 2 real
# (scrubbed from flowers-marketing, both tokens verified dead first), 41 the entries below.

librechat/*__tests__/*          # upstream fork (danny-avila/LibreChat), not Jason's code: generated PEM keypairs + the literal fixture token ghp_123456… inside CloudFront/MCP unit tests. Read 2026-08-08 S44.
librechat/*.test.ts             # upstream fork: packages/api/src/utils/key.test.ts — PEM fixtures feeding a key-parsing unit test. Read 2026-08-08 S44.
typingmind/src/_next/static/chunks/*.js   # upstream fork: vendored MINIFIED Next.js build output, never hand-edited here. Matches are documented placeholders — AWS's own documentation example key, the AKIA...EXAMPLE one (NOT spelled out here: G-E caught this very file when it was, 2026-08-08) and AIzaxxxxxx… Read 2026-08-08 S44.


Scripts/pan-redact.py   # the PAN redactor's OWN test corpus: MUST_REDACT holds the published fixture cards (4111…, 5555…, 3782…, 6011…, 4222… — Visa/MC/Amex/Discover documentation numbers, not issued to anyone) so the selftest can prove a miss leaks a card. A redactor with no card in its corpus cannot be drilled. First tripped 2026-09-08 smDrainDesk-14 (the file had not been committed since the PAN needle joined the sweep). Read 2026-09-08 smDrainDesk-14.

braatzio-plan/v3/tools/tenancy-scan.py   # same class as Scripts/pan-redact.py above: T1's own KNOWN_TEST_VECTORS set and --selftest fixtures hold the published Visa test PANs (4111…, 4242… — both published everywhere, issued to nobody) so the scanner's positive/negative controls can prove a real Luhn+issuer-prefix hit still flags while these two never do (smDrainLedger3-04's own incident was a lesson ABOUT one of them). A tenancy scanner that forbids card-shaped numbers cannot be drilled without a card-shaped number in it. First tripped 2026-09-27 sweepLedgerDrills i2 (SM 1217776851108137, unrelated content-sniffing change to the same file put these lines back in a diff hunk). Read 2026-09-27.

claude-blackbook/lessons/global/2026-08-24-guard-pinned-moving-subject-does-always.md   # the leaf that DOCUMENTS the PAN predicate's own tuning: it quotes 4111…1111, the universal Visa documentation number, as the single hit a tightened predicate (16 contiguous digits -> Luhn -> known BIN) returns tree-wide, i.e. the predicate's positive control written down. Verified 2026-09-21 gatewayFix-01: re-scanned the whole file, 7 Luhn-valid candidates, 6 are ASANA TASK GIDs (1217488…, 1210286…, 1215869…, 1215851…) that pass Luhn by coincidence and fail the BIN test, and the 7th is the Visa fixture. No issued card is present. Same class as Scripts/pan-redact.py above: a file about card handling cannot be drilled without a card in it. Tripped when the leaf was first re-committed after the PAN needle joined the sweep.

flowers-sms-concierge/daemon/test_redact.py   # the SMS concierge redactor's OWN unit-test corpus: it holds the published Stripe/Amex documentation cards (4242…4242, 3782…0005), issued to nobody, so the test can prove a card in an inbound text is redacted. Same class as Scripts/pan-redact.py above. Found by the estate-wide BIN+Luhn sweep 2026-10-09 ncFeynman1009pn (SM 1218616050378684): 50 repos, 32 hits, 0 issued cards.
flowers-sms-concierge/daemon/test_router_behavior.py   # router behavior test: a customer texts "charge her visa 4111…1111" and the test asserts the router never echoes the card. Published Visa test number, issued to nobody. Same sweep, 2026-10-09 ncFeynman1009pn.
voice-box/tools/test_pii_policy.py   # the PII policy's own test: a dictated message carrying the 4111…1111 Visa documentation number must be refused/redacted. Published test number. Same sweep, 2026-10-09 ncFeynman1009pn.
voice-box/tests/recency-drill.sh   # recency drill's synthetic transcript quotes 4111…1111 (Visa documentation number) as the "thing I keep forgetting" -- the drill proves a card-shaped memory is never resurfaced. Published test number. Same sweep, 2026-10-09 ncFeynman1009pn.
typingmind/src/lib/audio-recorder/js/*.min.js   # vendored MINIFIED WebAudioRecorder/LAME build (upstream, never hand-edited): the float constant .41421356…1832 (sqrt(2)-1) has no integer part, so the decimal rule does not blank it and its 16-digit fraction passes Luhn with a Visa IIN. Not a card. Same sweep, 2026-10-09 ncFeynman1009pn.
